The Yellow River is China’s second-longest river, known as the mother river of the Chinese nation. Originating from the Qinghai-Tibet Plateau, it runs through numerous provinces 
before emptying into the Bohai Sea. The fertile land in the Yellow River basin gave birth to ancient agricultural civilization. For thousands of years, the river has nourished 
